P1 (2026-11-11T10:12:11Z), before any v4 training, from existing scores only. Window choice against the DIA-NN RT (precursors with a right window, 2392 / 2400): winner right for D11 1971 / 2017, D11n 2166 / 2167, linear decoy-whitened LDA L11d 2266 / 2301, BASE 2278 / 2306. The linear readout on the same 11 features picks windows as well as BASE. The loss is in the tanh head of D11, which supports the saturation reading in MISSES_D11.md. Plan unchanged.
P2 (2026-11-11T11:00Z, after the phase 1 verdict; diagnostic, not a gated arm): `diag_readout.py` retrains D11 with the same seeds (reproduces scores_D11.npy, max abs diff 0) and splits s = z.w_z + tanh(g(z)).w_t. Window choice right (precursors with a window within 10 s of the DIA-NN RT, 2392 / 2400): D11 1971 / 2017, linear part alone 2255 / 2286, tanh part alone 1538 / 1545. The two parts are anti-correlated over all windows (r = -0.69 / -0.72); each has a larger variance than the sum (linear 1.26 / 1.54, tanh 1.81 / 1.95 of var(s)). The tanh part alone chooses windows worse than BASE, and it cancels part of the linear signal. A possible reading (not shown): the network part learns a correction that helps separate the top targets from decoys but hurts the choice among windows of one precursor. Candidate for a new plan: score windows for the within-precursor choice with the linear part (or penalise the tanh part's within-precursor variance), keeping one model.
